  "notes": "Drawn from 2025 photos of 737-800s, checked on an A330neo. The fin's band positions are measured on one photo and simplified to two light bands; the rear-fuselage bands are simplified (low confidence). The belly and the winglets' inner faces aren't seen squarely: the belly is taken as white. Colors by eye from overcast photos. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on PK-GFI (left, from ahead: too oblique for photo_trace's fit, so placed between the forward door and the overwing exits): the title runs about x 0.231 to 0.418 (lowercase 0.72 of the capitals), the bird logo just ahead of it centred x 0.20; its capitals reach y 0.75 (height 0.36; they had been drawn 0.25, visibly smaller than the photo's), baseline y 0.39 as drawn. The rear fuselage's sky-blue and teal edges are curves: smooth; the fin's bands are straight.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation. The 2009 'nature's wing' scheme (Landor Associates) replaced the 1985 Landor livery (white with the large Garuda bird on a dark blue tail)."
